# New pages under /client/* or /academy/* are nested-route children

Full detail: `docs/route-composition-conventions.md` (also read by Lovable).
Pointer only, from `AGENTS.md → Client Portal / Academy route composition`.

When adding a new page under `/client/*` or `/academy/*`:

1. Create the page component under `src/pages/client/` (or
   `src/pages/academy/` for Academy-only) with **no** layout wrapping — just
   the page's own content.
2. Add it as a child `<Route>` of the existing nested layout route in
   `src/routes/clientRoutes.tsx` or `src/routes/academyRoutes.tsx`, pointing
   at a `lazy()`-loaded import of the page.
3. **Do not** create a new `*Wrapper.tsx` file that does
   `<ClientLayout><MyPage /></ClientLayout>` (or `AcademyLayout`). That
   per-page-wrapper pattern was retired 2026-09-01 specifically because it
   forced the whole layout — sidebar state, a live realtime channel, the Ask
   Viv chat panel, a tenant/access check — to fully remount on every
   navigation between pages in the same portal. One new wrapper file
   silently breaks that persistence for every other page in the portal too.
4. Do not touch `ClientLayout.tsx`, `AcademyLayout.tsx`,
   `ClientLayoutRoute.tsx`, or `AcademyLayoutRoute.tsx` unless the task is
   specifically about the shared layout shell itself.

```text
❌ BAD:  src/pages/client/MyNewFeatureWrapper.tsx exporting
         <ClientLayout><MyNewFeaturePage /></ClientLayout>, registered as
         its own <Route> in App.tsx.

✅ GOOD: src/pages/client/MyNewFeaturePage.tsx with just the page content,
         added as <Route path="my-new-feature" element={<MyNewFeaturePage />} />
         inside the existing parent <Route path="/client" ...> in
         src/routes/clientRoutes.tsx.
```

Known gap, not a pattern to copy: several Academy pages under
`src/pages/academy/**` (courses list, certificates, workbooks, events,
community, the 3 PDP pages) predate this convention and still wrap
`AcademyLayout` themselves. Follow the rule above for new pages regardless.
